  "lang": "en",
  "description": [
    "A common, often “silent” liver disease. It resembles alcoholic liver disease, but occurs in people who drink little or no alcohol. The major feature in NASH is fat in the liver, along with inflammation and damage."
  ],
  "synonyms": [
    "NASH",
    "non alcoholic steatohepatitis",
    "nonalcoholic steatohepatitis"
  ],
